- Look, Mr. Tucker, I...
- We're through here.

16:54.146 --> 16:55.135
Get out of my house, Benji!

16:55.247 --> 16:58.182
Fine! If you're gonna be that way
about it, maybe I'll do this.

16:58.283 --> 16:59.910
- Yeah, look at this.
- Stop that!

17:00.019 --> 17:01.247
Yeah, you don't like this, huh?

17:01.353 --> 17:04.186
- This is what Benji would do.
- Stop doing that in my carpet!

17:04.289 --> 17:07.690
- Knock it off! Stop it!
- That feels so good.

17:09.261 --> 17:12.856
There's got to be a way to get back
at Jake Tucker for what he did to Chris.

17:12.965 --> 17:16.025
I know! Let's plant drugs in his locker.

17:16.135 --> 17:19.434
- Oh, my God! That's a great idea.
- Yeah, thought you'd like that.

17:19.538 --> 17:22.098
Hey, look at that Yosemite Sam mud flap.

17:22.207 --> 17:24.437
You had better stay back, Brian.

17:28.380 --> 17:29.369
I think we lost them.

17:30.682 --> 17:32.775
You stay here. I'm gonna go bury this film.

17:35.888 --> 17:38.356
Well, Mel Gibson,
this is one piece of crap...

17:38.457 --> 17:40.391
the world will never have to
suffer through.

17:41.326 --> 17:42.759
I am so clever.

17:42.861 --> 17:45.261
That's why they picked me
to convince Congress to go to war.

17:46.365 --> 17:49.391
There is no just cause
for an invasion of Iraq.

17:49.501 --> 17:52.299
Well, that may be.
But what we're all forgetting is...

17:52.404 --> 17:54.895
anyone who doesn't
want to go to war is gay.

17:55.007 --> 17:56.975
- I want to go to war.
- Yes.

17:57.076 --> 17:59.442
- We should definitely go.
- Yes, we should totally go to war.

17:59.545 --> 18:01.342
I was the first one who wanted to
go to war.

18:16.361 --> 18:17.487
Peter!

18:19.832 --> 18:21.356
Lois!

18:36.715 --> 18:39.946
Don't take this personally, Mrs. Griffin.
I'm doing this because I have to.

18:40.052 --> 18:41.314
What are you gonna do to me?

18:41.420 --> 18:43.012
What are you gonna do to me?

18:43.122 --> 18:46.285
As soon as your husband gives me
what I want, you're free to go.

18:46.391 --> 18:47.688
Anybody home?

18:48.327 --> 18:51.660
- Peter!
- All right, Gibson. I want my wife back.

18:51.763 --> 18:53.663
Or a woman
of equal physical attractiveness.

18:53.765 --> 18:54.959
Where's the film?

18:56.668 --> 19:00.229
- Come on, honey, let's get out of here.
- You're just gonna give him the film?

19:00.339 --> 19:02.398
Don't worry, Lois.
There's a dog turd in there.

19:02.508 --> 19:04.499
But by the time he finds out,
we'll be long...

19:04.610 --> 19:06.077
There's a dog turd in here.

19:06.545 --> 19:07.637
- Lois?
- What?

19:07.746 --> 19:08.838
Jump!

19:10.716 --> 19:11.740
No, wait!

19:11.850 --> 19:14.683
I'll deal with them myself.

19:21.994 --> 19:23.291
We're on top of the monument.

19:23.395 --> 19:24.555
Holy crap!

19:30.869 --> 19:33.497
You know, I know this is the wrong time
to be star struck...

19:33.605 --> 19:36.267
but Mel Gibson is shooting at us.

19:40.045 --> 19:42.036
Peter, help!

19:42.147 --> 19:44.377
Oh, man. I'm coming, Lois.

19:45.384 --> 19:47.648
Lois, look. I'm a booger.

19:48.220 --> 19:51.519
- Peter, for God's sake!
- Okay. Grab my hand.

19:53.992 --> 19:57.189
And now, Mr. Griffin, I want that film.

19:57.296 --> 20:00.754
Sure. It's right over there
in President Rushmore's mouth.

20:06.238 --> 20:09.435
My God! He just walked
right over the edge.

20:09.541 --> 20:12.942
Of course, he did.
Christians don't believe in gravity.

20:16.481 --> 20:19.473
- Peter, it's back.
- What, that rash?

20:19.585 --> 20:21.052
No, the spark.

20:21.153 --> 20:25.385
Honey, I have never been
more attracted to you than I am right now.

20:25.490 --> 20:26.923
Really? Wow!

20:27.025 --> 20:29.858
So I guess this honeymoon
was just the kind of excitement...

20:29.962 --> 20:31.190
our marriage needed.

20:31.330 --> 20:34.766
- I guess it just goes to show that you...
- Shut up and let's do it!

20:39.104 --> 20:41.470
Peter!
Yes!

20:41.573 --> 20:45.270
Hey, Jefferson, check it out.
A chick getting nailed on my head.

20:45.377 --> 20:48.540
Sweet. Hey, Teddy, pass the word
down to Frankenstein.

20:48.714 --> 20:49.976
Oh, ha-ha!

20:51.817 --> 20:54.411
<i>In local news, a Buddy Cianci
Junior High School student...</i>

20:54.519 --> 20:56.714
<i>has been arrested for possession of drugs.</i>

20:56.822 --> 20:59.791
<i>The student has been sentenced
to 200 hours of community service...</i>

20:59.891 --> 21:01.620
<i>and is a very bad boy.</i>

21:01.727 --> 21:04.924
<i>We now go to Ollie Williams for the
punishment forecast. Ollie?</i>

21:05.030 --> 21:06.497
<i>- He gonna get it!
- Thanks, Ollie.</i>

21:06.598 --> 21:07.565
<i>Now this.</i>

21:07.666 --> 21:09.657
So you actually put coke
in that kid's locker?

21:09.768 --> 21:11.258
- Yup.
- Where'd you get it?

21:11.370 --> 21:12.337
I got a guy.

21:12.437 --> 21:15.895
Don't let it get the best of you.
I used to be a lawyer.

21:16.008 --> 21:19.068
See you next week.
Good to be back, America.

21:19.069 --> 22:20.069
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru